{"run_id": "20260815T104348-hepkg-48523", "qid": "gen-concept-a45b17fa", "repeat": 1, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "ebcca58d5d8f", "git_sha": "b6ce7b2-dirty", "question": "Count the analyses that measured f_CP^Htt (Htt CP-odd effective fractional cross section).", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "merged_entities"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 1 analysis that measures an observable related to \"f_CP^Htt\" (Htt CP-odd effective fractional cross section). This analysis is titled:\n\n**\"$CP$ Properties of Higgs Boson Interactions with Top Quarks in the $t\\bar{t}H$ and $tH$ Processes Using $H\\rightarrow\\gamma\\gamma$ with the ATLAS Detector\"**\n\nThe exact quote from the paper that supports this measurement is:\n\n> \"The $t\\bar{t}H$ signal strength (measured relative to the Standard Model expectation) is determined in the $H \\rightarrow \\gamma\\gamma$ decay channel.\"\n\nTherefore, the graph records 1 analysis that measures the observable related to the CP properties of the Higgs boson interactions with top quarks, specifically the $t\\bar{t}H$ signal strength.\n\nAnswer:\nThe graph records 1 analysis that measured f_CP^Htt (Htt CP-odd effective fractional cross section).\nAnswerable: true\nReason: answered", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2103.04956", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2208.12095", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2504.13081", "2510.07527", "2602.18611", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "f_CP^Htt", "kind": "observable"}, "rows": 42, "error": null, "seconds": 93.528}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "result_measures_observable", "object_set": "set_1_kept"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.006}, {"round": 3, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "result_measures_observable", "object_set": "s